From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 02:15:43 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 048/342] package kit: repositories may hold packages of other
 vendors

BRepositoryWriter refused packages whose vendor differs from the
repository's. A port's own repository holds Haiku's packages, ported
software and applications from several vendors, and nothing that reads
repositories relies on one vendor; HaikuDepot shows each package's
vendor as its publisher.

Tested: package_repo creates the ODROID-C2 port's repository of 38
packages from 11 vendors.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/kits/package/hpkg/RepositoryWriterImpl.cpp | 11 +++--------
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/kits/package/hpkg/RepositoryWriterImpl.cpp b/src/kits/package/hpkg/RepositoryWriterImpl.cpp
index aba31387c2..9996c5ccf6 100644
--- a/src/kits/package/hpkg/RepositoryWriterImpl.cpp
+++ b/src/kits/package/hpkg/RepositoryWriterImpl.cpp
@@ -401,14 +401,9 @@ RepositoryWriterImpl::_RegisterCurrentPackageInfo()
 		return B_NAME_IN_USE;
 	}
 
-	// all packages must have the same vendor as the repository
-	const BString& expectedVendor = fRepositoryInfo->Vendor();
-	if (fPackageInfo.Vendor().ICompare(expectedVendor) != 0) {
-		fListener->PrintError("package '%s' has unexpected vendor '%s' "
-			"(expected '%s')!\n", fPackageInfo.Name().String(),
-			fPackageInfo.Vendor().String(), expectedVendor.String());
-		return B_BAD_DATA;
-	}
+	// Packages from other vendors than the repository's are fine: a port's
+	// own repository holds Haiku, ported software and applications, and
+	// nothing that reads repositories relies on one vendor.
 
 	// all packages must have an architecture that's compatible with the one
 	// used by the repository
